Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.37,0:00:06.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}What kind of motion can\Ngrow a {\c&H3468EB&}magnetic field{\c&HF7F4F2&}?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.12,0:00:12.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}In a perfect conductor, field lines\Nwould be threads frozen into the fluid.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.37,0:00:16.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Wherever the {\c&HE58739&}flow{\c&HF7F4F2&} stretches a thread,\Nthe field along it grows stronger.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.68,0:00:21.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Real metals let the threads\Nsmudge, like spreading ink.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.54,0:00:25.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The smudging speed is set by the\Nmetal's {\c&H7AAF1B&}magnetic diffusivity{\c&HF7F4F2&}.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.47,0:00:27.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Same flow, two metals.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.92,0:00:31.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A good conductor smudges slowly:\Nthe threads stay sharp.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.14,0:00:36.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}A poor one smudges fast:\Nthe threads blur away.
